// the parameters of the contract
Fact caretaker
Fact child
Fact start-date       Identified by Int
Fact initial-allowance  Identified by Int

// time management
Fact date Identified by Int // keeps track of current date, counting the days 

Event tick // ticking of the clock, with 1 day intervals
  Terminates date // terminates the current date
  Creates date(date + 1) // but only after a new date has been created based on it

Fact days Identified by Int

Event start-the-clock
  Related to days 
  Creates date(days)

// the following invariants formalize the assumption that a caretaker contract is always between exactly one child and one caretaker, although multiple such contracts can co-exists, e.g. one child with multiple caretakers and one caretaker with multiple children.
Invariant at-most-one-child Where (Forall child, child' : child == child')
Invariant at-most-one-caretaker Where (Forall caretaker, caretaker': caretaker == caretaker')

// Article 1
// The following formalization shows a coarse degree of granularity, relying on separate policy formalizations of the specific rules set by the caretaker

Fact rule 

// The power to set rules
Act set-rule
  Actor caretaker
  Recipient child
  Related to rule
  Creates rule // the given rule is made to hold (be in place)
  Holds when child && caretaker // the two parties have entered the contract

// The duty to obey rules
Duty my-roof-my-rules
  Holder child
  Claimant caretaker
  Holds when child && caretaker
  Violated when disobeys()
  // implicitly: 
  // Violated when (Exists rule: disobeys(child, rule))

Fact disobeys Identified by child * rule
// The `disobeys` fact signals violation of the my-roof-my-rules duty for a specific rule
// An external monitoring system should be in place to detect these violations
// and creates instances of this fact

// Article 2

// The power to enforce rules, by grounding
Act ground
  Actor caretaker
  Recipient child
  Related to days 
  Creates grounded(date = date + days) // grounded until `date + days` 
  Terminates disobeys // after punishment, no longer in violation
  Holds when Violated(my-roof-my-rules) // there exists a violation of the mentioned duty
          && days <= 28

Fact grounded Identified by child * date.

// extend the effects of the clock to ensure termination
// this is done as a modular extension using the `Extend` keyword  
Extend Event tick
  Terminates grounded When date + 1 == grounded.date.

// Article 3 
Fact allowance Identified by Int
Fact amount    Identified by Int
  Derived from allowance-obligation.amount // allows system to iterate these
Placeholder payment-date For date

Duty allowance-obligation
  Holder caretaker
  Claimant child
  Related to payment-date, amount
  Violated when payment-date < date 

// The ticking of the clock also creates payment obligations for the new week
.
Extend Event tick // create allowance-obligation for the next week
  Creates allowance-obligation(payment-date=date+7,amount=allowance)
    When (date - start-date) % 7 == 0.

Act pay
  Actor caretaker
  Recipient child
  Related to payment-date, amount'
  Terminates allowance-obligation() When amount' >= amount // duty is terminated when enough is paid
  Holds when date >= start-date
          && (payment-date - start-date) % 7 == 0

// Article 4
Act ask-for-help
  Actor child
  Recipient caretaker
  Related to homework
  Creates obligation-to-help(demand-date=date)
  Holds when date >= start-date

Fact demand-date Identified by Int
  Derived from obligation-to-help.demand-date

Placeholder duedate For date
Fact homework Identified by duedate

Duty obligation-to-help
  Holder caretaker
  Claimant child
  Related to demand-date, homework
  Violated when date > homework.duedate 

Act help-with-homework
  Actor caretaker
  Recipient child
  Related to homework
  Terminates obligation-to-help()
  Holds when obligation-to-help()

// Article 5
Act refuse-to-help
  Actor caretaker
  Recipient child
  Related to homework
  Terminates obligation-to-help() When demand-date >= homework.duedate - 1
  Holds when obligation-to-help() &&   demand-date >= homework.duedate - 1 

// Article 6
Act demand-allowance-increase
  Actor child
  Recipient caretaker
  Terminates allowance
            ,obligation-to-help
  Creates allowance(allowance + (allowance * 2) / 10)
  Holds when (Exists obligation-to-help: Violated(obligation-to-help))
